<title>SWITZERLAND: Feldschloesschen gives IT business to IBM.</title>
<headline>Feldschloesschen gives IT business to IBM.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss brewing and mineral water group Feldschloesschen-Huerlimann Holding AG (FHH) has given International Business Machines Corp's Swiss subsidiary its entire information technology business, IBM said.</p>
<p>IBM will employ the nearly 40 workers who had run the business for FHH. The outsourcing contract, which takes effect on October 1, covers volume of around 65 million Swiss francs, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>It gave no financial details.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
